# Maintaining accepted substitutions

`variant_ids.json` is the only accepted mapping. The manual helper reports candidates
and never rewrites it. Normal recommendation updates do not perform variant discovery.

1. Discover candidates with `python scripts/build_bulk_variant_ids.py --search '<regex>'`.
   It reads one Weird Gloop catalog; `--catalog <file>` reuses a local download.
2. Verify each item's functionality and versions using Weird Gloop and Wiki infoboxes.
   Similar names or models do not establish equivalence. Exclude placeholders, noted
   items, and restricted-game variants from ordinary equipment substitutions.
3. Edit the existing JSON structure. `base_id` and `extra_ids` define accepted IDs;
   `name` and `note` document the decision. Add a source URL to `note`.
4. Use optional `preference` only for verified ordering within a comparable recommendation.
   Larger values are preferred. Same-tier cosmetics share a value. An upgraded item
   must never accept a weaker item. Keep chains explicit and complete; the validator
   rejects incomplete chains rather than inferring further substitutions.
5. Use optional `slot` to constrain a known equipment mapping (for example `cape`).
   Broad mixed-family recommendations retain their original order and do not acquire
   inferred upgrades. Inspect the actual generated diff for unexpected contexts.
6. Do not add broken/non-equipable IDs to wearable alternatives. Existing Wiki source
   IDs remain intact. Repair-state source entries may accept usable substitutes but
   must not make the reverse relationship valid. Quiver ammo recovery also depends on
   account unlocks, which an ID cannot prove.
7. Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` before generating data.
8. Regenerate recommendations when requested. Mapping additions can use
   `python apply_variants.py`; removals need fresh raw scrape output first, because
   previously expanded JSON has no provenance identifying old added IDs.
9. Review source/mapping changes separately from generated recommendations. Confirm
   that activity/style/slot/tier structure is unchanged, additions are accepted, and
   every removal is explained. Repeat expansion must be byte-stable.

Lookup: https://chisel.weirdgloop.org/moid/item_name.html and
https://chisel.weirdgloop.org/moid/item_id.html . See README.md for usage and limitations.
